    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the salutation feature following the existing derived-field conventions in this Spring Boot PetClinic app.\n\nThe request may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR); the owner now exposes a derived `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, falling back to just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges:\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, plus a derived `getSalutation()` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or `lastName` when the title is null/blank.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` as an optional input property on `OwnerFields`, and `salutation` as a read-only derived property on `Owner`. The DTOs are generated from this spec, so MapStruct auto-maps `title` (input) and `salutation` (output) with no mapper changes needed.\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `title` column so the value persists across create \u2192 get. Tests run on the `hsqldb` profile.\n\nThe new `Cp45Tests` and all 55 pre-existing tests pass.",
